01. S3 + Lambda Real-Time Example
Suppose users upload images.

User
 |
 | upload image
 v
S3
 |
 | ObjectCreated event
 v
Lambda
 |
 +-- Resize image
 +-- Generate thumbnail
 +-- Store thumbnail

This is a classic serverless architecture.



02. S3 + CloudTrail
You can use AWS CloudTrail to audit API activity.

Example:

Developer
    |
    | DeleteObject
    v
   S3
    |
    v
 CloudTrail

You can investigate:

Who accessed the bucket?
Who deleted an object?
When did it happen?
Which API was called?




03. S3 Access Logs:
S3 can also provide logging mechanisms for bucket access.

A common architecture:

Application Bucket
       |
       | logs
       v
Logging Bucket

Keep logging data separate from the application data where appropriate.




04. S3 Replication:
S3 supports replication between buckets.

For example:

Region: Mumbai
     |
     | Replication
     v
Region: Singapore

Example:

Mumbai S3
   |
   | CRR
   v
Singapore S3

CRR = Cross-Region Replication

Useful for scenarios such as:

Disaster recovery
Compliance
Geographic requirements
Business continuity


05. Same-Region Replication:
You can also replicate within the same AWS Region:

Bucket A
   |
   | SRR
   v
Bucket B

SRR = Same-Region Replication
